  1424                              <1> ; The skip cache (base). Nearly every skip is one that has happened before
  1425                              <1> ; (a loop skips the same false block on every pass), so the first scan from
  1426                              <1> ; each place is remembered: 64 entries of {start, end} at skc, found by the
  1427                              <1> ; start's low 6 bits. Only skips that start inside the program text are kept
  1428                              <1> ; (the line buffer changes, and so may the heap); the cache is emptied
  1429                              <1> ; whenever a run starts (run0). A program that changes its own text while it
